        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Hangzhou</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 221 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Established as the county of Qiantang by the First Emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a>, in 221 or 222 BCE; made the seat of the prefecture of Hang under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> in 589 CE, from which the name Hangzhou came.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">At the southern end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a> and the head of Hangzhou Bay, north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qiantang-river">Qiantang River</a> and beside West Lake, in northwestern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> capital Lin'an; West Lake and the causeways of Bai Juyi and Su Shi; the southern end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a>; a population said to have made it the largest city in the world; accounts by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoric-of-pordenone">Odoric of Pordenone</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a>; Longjing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a>; the fires of the Song city</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Hangzhou is the capital and most populous city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a> province and a sub-provincial city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze River</a> Delta.</span></div>
